A||||63||JAMIE||Fieroshop and Tgowens - where is my money?||||1||
Z||000000||JAMIE||04-22-2001||10:02 AM||||Too bad it has to come to this - I have tried to keep this private but enough is enough. I have asked a number of times for you to credit my credit card for the $300 purchase price for the seat covers you sold me that came from George's car. I purchased these with the explicit understanding that I could return them if I was not satisfied with them. Well, I returned them 1 day after I received them - this was well before Christmas - and still no refund - the only response of any sort I received was from Terry saying that he is "not liable for anything the Fiero Shop does" - so how do I interpret that response?<P>Guys, for the first several months of waiting I was surprised and disappointed. Now I am just angry. I will wait no longer - confirm that you have credited my credit card.<P>Again, it is unfortunate that this issue could not remain private.Fiero Shop, please post response here so that fellow Forum members will know that you have corrected this problem. For the record, I have purchased parts from many many many vendors (Fiero Shop included) and have never had a problem - I'm not a complainer nor am I unreasonable - in fact,I invite all parts vendors who I have ever dealt with to post here any problems they have ever had in their dealings with me. <P>George/Terry - please fix this problem.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||04-22-2001||05:32 PM||||Stupid question but did you talk to George Miller on the phone about this? My past experience with him is that he usually will solve your problem if you call him directly.<P>Toll free @ 866-534-8486<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 04-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||04-22-2001||06:20 PM||||Jamie, as I have said repeatedly, I am not responsible for the Fiero Shop in either a financial or legal manner. All I can do is forward messages to George (the shop owner) for him to act on. I have done so and as such, have done all that I can do. I do know that there were problems with the credit transaction equipment and subsequently the credit service company had been contacted about these problems (returns were being charged a second time rather than treated as a return).<P>I will say this, now that you have made this a public issue. You returned the seat covers by saying that you were dissatisfied with them because they had burn marks, etc. I did inspect those seat covers (which had been covered with sheepskin covers while in the car) and found not one single burn mark or flaw on them. True they could have used a cleaning but they were not sold as new but rather as used items. However, we told you, as is the policy, that if you were dissatisfied to simply return them for credit.<P>I will speak to George about this again but, you might want to take 88formula's advice and call George about this........the toll free number is 866-534-8486||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||04-23-2001||01:54 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by tgowens:<BR><B>return them for credit.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Man... That Sucks...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> $300 in credit to a place your mad at & probably wont order from again..<P>I dont have anything bad to say about The Fiero Shop.... But their prices are VERY high. (Just my 2 cents) I needed a dash awhile back & they wanted over $300 for one. (Not even shipped) <BR><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A>||||reg||11
Z||000004||Cameron||04-23-2001||02:12 AM||||I personally have nothing but good things to say about the Fiero Shop.  They have done a great job on the work I needed done to my '87 GT and my previous '88 Formula.  I would like to know if you have spoken to George about this.  Whenever I had a problem, go straight to George and he'd fix it right away.  Terry doesn't have control over the business.  You cannot hold him liable for anything the Fiero Shop does.  Oh well, I guess that's all.<P><P>------------------<BR>Cameron<BR> <A HREF="http://Fiero.NetMARC.com" TARGET=_blank>http://Fiero.NetMARC.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||tgowens||04-23-2001||02:33 AM||||Carl, if I remember correctly you were looking for a <I>perfect</I> as in <I>mint</I> BLACK dashboard - as you may be aware - there are not too many of those around. I'm sorry you feel the prices are too high but we have to take into consideration the cost to us as well as maintain or profit level.<P>Add to that the fact that these pieces are not made any longer - more Fiero parts are discontinued every day - and once supply is depleted that is the end of it. Honestly, I don't think that $300 for a perfect mint black dashboard was too high but, that's just MY opinion.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Haze_Performance||04-23-2001||02:44 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by tgowens:<BR><B>Carl, if I remember correctly you were looking for a <I>perfect</I> as in <I>mint</I> BLACK dashboard - as you may be aware - there are not too many of those around. I'm sorry you feel the prices are too high but we have to take into consideration the cost to us as well as maintain or profit level.<P>Add to that the fact that these pieces are not made any longer - more Fiero parts are discontinued every day - and once supply is depleted that is the end of it. Honestly, I don't think that $300 for a perfect mint black dashboard was too high but, that's just MY opinion.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey tgowens,<BR>  Im not tring to bad mouth ya.. And your right I was looking for a perfect dash.. But just to let you know.. I found 2 here on the forum for under $100. Both were black & perfect. I know that most Fiero parts are not made anymore but there still just Fieros.. A lot of people act like these cars are gold plated. <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A>||||reg||10
Z||000007||tgowens||04-23-2001||02:50 AM||||I understand -- you also realize that most of the time prices are higher west of the Rockies..........but, as I have said before -- I don't set the prices - I just work here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> (was it REALLY $300? -- I'll agree, that IS high!)||||reg||1
Z||000008||84Bill||04-23-2001||08:18 AM||||Remind me to never use the Fiero Shop for anything!||||reg||8
Z||000009||fierojunky||04-23-2001||08:38 AM||||84 Bill - did you have a bad experience with the Fiero Shop - because if your comment was based on others opinions about the shop there are many people here who will back the shop.  Personally - ever time i ordered stuff through the Fiero SHop i have gotten great service and the parts where delivered right away.  Even if the parts are alittle more expensive i still order them through the Fiero Shop because i know i'll get them - and i'm getting them from other Fiero lovers not someone who is disgused the car is still running.  So unless you personally have had bad experiences with a vendor whether it is the Fiero Shop, the Fiero Store etc.  I suggest everyone quit bashing the vendors on our side.  ||||reg||13
Z||000010||Taijiguy||04-23-2001||09:46 AM||||This isn't any kind of narrative on the Fiero Shop, since I have no direct experience with them (aside from finding their prices high) But then there are alot of other people out there as well who try to rape us on parts prices as well. That's free enterprise. If the prices are too high for me, I find them elsewhere, and there is ALWAYS an elsewhere. Otherwise I go without, or excerise my imagination, and make due. To me, on the subject of price, it's how much effort a person is willing to put out to find the part at a better price. When a business can no longer sell parts or services at a set price, they either have to evaluate their pricing, or accept the lack of sales. <BR>I personally appreciate information on businesses that promote their goods here. Good and bad. At least here, businesses are afforded the opportunity to defend their actions. Although, in this case all I've seen is disclaimers and refusals of responsibility. In all fairness Terry, you seem to be a proud voice for the Fiero Shop, it's reasonable that people will associate you with them, including for complaints. Sorry, but this thing with the credit billing system just don't seem right. I can see the system being down for a couple of days, but since December? (things that make you go "hmmmmm")<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Alex4mula||04-23-2001||10:28 AM||||I would like to see this problem clarified. I personally ordered a Kevlar clutch last year from George. It arrived as expected and I can only say it is great. Excellent grip and smooth. One year now with my 3.4 & I love it. When you hear bad things from many persons about a business then you should start wondering why. One or two here or there could be isolated cases. Anyway this one should be clarified for good. I haven't seen Fieroshop post in a long time.||||reg||1
Z||000012||TRL46202||04-23-2001||11:23 AM||||Jamie, You did say you put that on a credit card? If so call the card co. and disput the amount and since you did return the item the card co. will go after them. Just a thought. <P>Tom||||reg||1
Z||000013||fieroshop||04-23-2001||11:23 AM||||I had e-mailed Jamie of list. But having talked to Terry He told me that Jamie was supposed to have a store credit and not a refund.<BR>I had not recieved anything from Jamie on this issue and have not talked to him.<BR>All I can say is some people like to air their laundry in public instead of contacting the person in charge.<BR>I have no reason not to give Jamie his store credit. The seat covers that he returned were perfect and he knows it.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||84Bill||04-23-2001||12:37 PM||||Junkey<BR>Nope never have delt with them but like any other "service" or lack there of is more typical theese days, it only takes 1 bad situation to sour the expierence. I would like to thank the individual who created this thread because IT SHEDS light on how "some" customers are treated. Now you say "how can I be concerned about other ppls situations and not know first hand". Well lets just say I HAVE 300 bucks to spend unlike the poor guy who just wants his money back. I would rather not take the chance and be out 300 bucks know what I mean? Thats why I said I will not ever deal with them because the have violated the TRUST of a fellow customer and Fiero owner. Its a shame how companies treat their customes theese days and The Fiero Shop should bend over backwards to help this guy out no questions asked. Right???? I thaught so because the customer is always right, blaaahahahahah !!!! thats a good one.<P>And besides as a consumer I have the right to my opinions and to share those opinions with whome I choose. You call it bashing well thats just your opinion and yes I'll bash anything I feel needs my particular brand of bashing. <BR>I dont play around when it comes to stuff like this (MONEY) even if it they were the ONLY fiero parts store in the world and trust me I love my fiero but not to the point of just throwing away money. So let me say it like this. I have a voice and I will be heard weather or not anyone listens. I will not deal with the Fiero Shop I don't like their policies <BR>ok Junkie<P>Fiero Shop <BR>I saw your responce and it was noted that he has store credit, well for me that would not do. The way I see "Store Credit" is that we have your money no matter what and you MUST buy from us again. so put another way " Oh you dont like OUR seat covers well Tough Sh!t now you don't have money to shop elsewhere" and thats lame. Again thats just the way things are now days. Its all about the bottom dollar not the customer but his or her money and the best way to get it and keep it.<P>Ok nuff said I have aired my bit and I hope I have made so sort of difference here. Maybe now something might change maybe not (typical) <BR>I can garentee this, I know I have made enemys today just for voicing my opinion, kinda stupid isn't it.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 04-23-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000015||fierojunky||04-23-2001||01:41 PM||||*hands 84Bill his binky* Like i said - i wouldn't base my opinions of a vendor who has dedicated their business in an interest we all share on a few isolated incidents; especially if you never had any dealings with them.  If i had a negative experience with a vendor - sure i would look elsewhere to do my business.   <P>------------------<BR>caulked, locked and ready to rock||||reg||1
Z||000016||stimpy||04-23-2001||02:21 PM||||84Bill, although I totally respect your freedom to state your opinion, I think you would be hard pressed to find any vendor or business that someone doesn't have a gripe about. That's just the cost of doing business.  I trust that this is resolvable.||||reg||1
Z||000017||jlruiz67||04-23-2001||03:24 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by tgowens:<BR><B>Jamie, as I have said repeatedly, I am not responsible for the Fiero Shop in either a financial or legal manner. All I can do is forward messages to George (the shop owner) for him to act on. I have done so and as such, have done all that I can do. I do know that there were problems with the credit transaction equipment and subsequently the credit service company had been contacted about these problems (returns were being charged a second time rather than treated as a return).<P>I will say this, now that you have made this a public issue. You returned the seat covers by saying that you were dissatisfied with them because they had burn marks, etc. I did inspect those seat covers (which had been covered with sheepskin covers while in the car) and found not one single burn mark or flaw on them. True they could have used a cleaning but they were not sold as new but rather as used items. However, we told you, as is the policy, that if you were dissatisfied to simply return them for credit.<P>I will speak to George about this again but, you might want to take 88formula's advice and call George about this........the toll free number is 866-534-8486</B>[/QUOTE<P>Hello tgowens<P>     Small point that you may want to consider, under author when you post: <BR>tgowens<BR>Member <BR>Posts: 1419<BR>From:Fiero Shop - Richmond, CA USA - toll free - 866-534-8486<BR>Registered: Apr 2000 <P>And on your post you state that you work at the shop and you will talk to George.<P>Well you state that: " I am not responsible for the Fiero Shop in either a financial or legal manner"<BR>You are correct, you are probably not responsible but you are acting as an agent of the  Fiero Shop, I haven't seen a post from the Fiero Shop asking you to stop speaking for them and you state that you work there so legaly you are the Fiero Shop and the Fiero Shop has to comply with what you offer Fiero Shop costumers. I personally think that this might have been a misunderstanding and I'm sure that George at the Fiero shop will provide a full refund. My coment here is so you understand that you are presenting your self as an agent of Fiero Shop.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000018||84Bill||04-23-2001||03:40 PM||||Thank you Stimpy and Junkey for allowing me to air my opinion. <BR>My position still has not changed except that I may possibly at some time down the road possibly do buisness with the Fiero Shop but I doubt it. Because I don't want credit I want MONEY for returned merchendise thats all. Not to mention Terry's (please understand Terry) attitude tward this guy I hate that "sorry man I just work here" krap He represents the Fiero Shop and is a lot closer to the folks in charge than I am so unless they decide to change this policy then what can I say other than... <BR>I won't be buying anything from the Fiero Shop||||reg||6
Z||000019||fyerstarter||04-23-2001||03:55 PM||||Store credit is a joke. The guy has $300 to buy some seat covers, so he bought some seat covers and doesn't like the seat covers The Fieroshop has to offer. Now what is he going to do with his store credit? Buy a dashboard!? He doesn't need a dash, or a clutch, or some doorpanels, HE NEEDS SEAT COVERS! Whether or not you think the covers are in mint condition seems irrellevant to me, they're not going on your car and your not the one forking out the cash for them. <P>It seems like a pretty simple concept to me. Seat Covers=$300, your sent him covers and he sent you $300, now he sent back the same covers so then he should get back the same $300 right? Im sure the seat covers did not accumulate any wear or depreciate in value during the short time that he had them. It can't get much simpler than that can it?<p>[This message has been edited by fyerstarter (edited 04-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||tgowens||04-23-2001||03:59 PM||||jlruiz67, point noted and corrected......<P>84Bill, you are entitled to your opinions, and you can certainly buy from who you want just as I do - sorry if you think that "I'm sorry, I just work here is (as you put it) "krap". The fact of the matter is this - I work <I>with</I> George, not <I>for</I> George, meaning, I am not in his employ nor am I paid by him. I have made that abundantly clear many times and either people can't read or understand what it is that I am saying.<P>The legal entity is" George Miller dba Fiero Shop - I am not legally not financially an agent for this shop and am doing nothing more than helping a friend when I make any statements regarding this shop - much the same as many of you do on here when you mention a "friend" who has a part or a car or can do something for a Fiero..........how doing things personally for a friend got to big such a big blow-up I'll never know. I have met many of you and you all know my status here and not once have I done anything to draw such ire from anyone. I have made an attempt at being helpful to others here and I do what I can to impart information when I happen to know the answer.......<P>Enough said and I am gone from here!||||reg||1
Z||000021||RobertVol||04-23-2001||04:06 PM||||Cliff<P>This may not even be possible but instead of these things being aired out on the normal posts were everyone can ...get into a Cyber Pissing contest about who is right and wrong,<BR>And frankly I am sick of it. (most may be legit but other stuff looks childish) <P>My suggestion if possible...set up something like Ebay and let people rate the service of the vendor. List all the vendors and let the members leave a notation about the service they received. I feel this would get rid of all this crap back 'n forth. <P>It may not be worth the time or even possible but its a thought. <P>You already have a link at the bottom to the vendors for parts, right?<P>At least then its in a controlled posting. Limit the post to a certain amount number of words. Then they can say good or bad and why and THATS it! <P>BTW..Jamie not a knock on you at all just saw this one first and made me think. Because of all the other posts going back in forth recently. <P><BR>Anyway ...opinions? <P><P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club<P>CLICK BELOW AND SEE OUR SITE !!! <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=819451&a=5959473&p=36934984&Sequence=1"> ||||reg||1
Z||000022||Bob Englert||04-23-2001||05:58 PM||||I am not sure that a separate section is needed for this type of post.<P>The beauty of the forum is that if you don't want to read, don't click on the topic!  This is why I am using the forum more and the e-mail lists less and less.<P>I understand that in business that it is very hard to keep everyone happy all the time.  I also understand that there is always 2 sides to every story.  <P>I personally do like to know about these types of issues.  1 post will not seriously affect if I deal with that vendor, but if some number of Fiero owners start sharing similar stories, I want to know so as to find other vendors if possible.  This is why I would never order parts though FOCOA.<P>I hope the problem is resolved to everyone's satisfaction.<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl<p>[This message has been edited by Bob Englert (edited 04-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000023||88formula||04-23-2001||06:16 PM||||You know I have learned that when someone has had a good experience that this person usually only tells a few people about it but if that person has had a bad experience that they then tell a thousand people and make it seem worse than it really was. <P>Have you contacted George Miller by phone and let him know of your problem before you went on here and made a public issue of it or did you skip that part? I bet you didn’t!  <P><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000024||88formula||04-23-2001||06:32 PM||||Maybe some day Wal-Mart will enter the tiny little fiero market and offer you penny pinching whiner’s cheap parts for cheap money and put everyone else in the fiero business out of business.  Than you can enjoy your cheap parts with crappy service and the next time you need advice about fiero’s you can just ask the knowledgeable Wal-Mart sales representative and they will be glade to help you with that difficult question.  <P>Remember you get what you pay for and when the supply doesn't meet the demand things get expensive. I have bought many things from George and I can tell you that his service is great and fast and the parts I got were excellent. I have talked to him many times on the phone and don't think he is in this business to screw us.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000025||Jay||04-23-2001||11:24 PM||||I don't know George and I've never ordered from the shop, but I do own my own business.  It is sad when customer and service provider can't come to an agreement.  Some people (and  I'm not saying it is anyone here) can't be satisfied, no matter what you do.  On the other hand a business (especially a service business) should bend over backwards to preserve their reputation.  Sometimes that means doing things for free or taking a loss.  When you go the extra mile for your customers you will undoubtibly gain many more.  I've got several referals from people I would never have expected them from because I made sure the customer was happy, bottom line.  If the customer is not happy with an "in store" credit, action must be taken.  At the same time each situation deserves its own appraisal.  Waiting for a refund or credit since December is unacceptable.  I hope everything is resolved because there are very few good shops that can provide us with the parts and service that we need, and from what I hear, the Fiero Shop has proven itself to be a good company.  All businesses will experience some bad press, if they say they have never had a complaint then they are lying.  The correct thing to look for is if it becomes a trend...<P>My opinion as someone who is self employed.<P>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000026||84Bill||04-24-2001||12:15 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Bob Englert:<BR><B>I am not sure that a separate section is needed for this type of post.<P>The beauty of the forum is that if you don't want to read, don't click on the topic!  This is why I am using the forum more and the e-mail lists less and less.<P>I understand that in business that it is very hard to keep everyone happy all the time.  I also understand that there is always 2 sides to every story.  <P>I personally do like to know about these types of issues.  1 post will not seriously affect if I deal with that vendor, but if some number of Fiero owners start sharing similar stories, I want to know so as to find other vendors if possible.  This is way I would never order parts though FOCOA.<P>I hope the problem is resolved to everyone's satisfaction.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thank you Bob<BR> I do agree with you this is a great forum and yes things sometimes get childish BUT this is not the case (this thread) ||||reg||6
Z||000027||fieroshop||04-24-2001||01:13 AM||||Why all this nonsense that is going on.<BR>1: I have never been contacted and to this date with everything going on Jamie has not been man enough to call me on my toll free number that has been posted.<P>I have never received an e-mail from him and until he calls me I will play dumb.<BR>Yes this is workable but has to be by the parties involved and not by the forum.<BR>When and if he ever calls then I will settle this with him and not with anybody else and as far as I am concerned it is nobodies business but his and mine.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
