Z||000030||buds||04-24-2001||09:08 AM||||Why play dumb. Ya should have done right when you first read this topic. I will personally never deal with a supplier that plays these games, thats just poor customer service imo.||||reg||1
Z||000031||RobertVol||04-24-2001||09:10 AM||||My point exactly...<P>If you want to know that there may be a problem on a vendor have a list were you can check the good with the bad, but most of these posts become mud slinging contests. <P>I have never purchased from George but have called him a while back concerning an EGR issue and when I called for things he probably could have sold me something, but he took the time to explain a few things to look for, that it may be something a normal mechanic may not see since not being Fiero Experienced. George was right. Saved a few hundred. So since we are going back in forth ...here is some good news on George......<P><BR>This proves what 88Formula said above. I didnt mention it because it wasnt bad it was good. My fault <P>So George you probably dont remember but Thanks <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club<P>CLICK BELOW AND SEE OUR SITE !!! <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=819451&a=5959473&p=36934984&Sequence=1"> ||||reg||14
Z||000032||fieroshop||04-24-2001||09:20 AM||||Bud, since obviously you know nothing about what is really happening you should not say anything. As far as playing dumb, I did not and had you read my first answer in the begining you would see that I made a statement that I had answered Jamie directly and not thru the forum.<BR>It makes no difference if you do business with me or not. I do have a good reputation and I intenet to keep that up. I prefer to deal directly with people and not thru a public forum. <BR>I am in touch with Jamie and this is our business and does not concern you or anybody else on this forum.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000033||GodSend||04-24-2001||09:33 AM||||Why do we bother having a forum then?  There are many people which view this kind of information as one of the most valuable on the forum.  <P>If you really do feel you have done nothing wrong, then let this thread exist and trust that everyone will see that this guy is being unreasonable.  The only reason I could see for someone not wanting this thread is if they are hiding something.||||reg||1
Z||000034||Taijiguy||04-24-2001||09:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fieroshop:<BR><B>I am in touch with Jamie and this is our business and does not concern you or anybody else on this forum.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Unfortunately, as a business owner myself I can safely say that while you may feel that way, most potential customers will see it differently. They are interested in knowing how a business handles probelms, regardless of their nature, be it a reasonable complaint, or and unreasonable customer. (And I'm not trying to indicate which is the case here) I spent a great deal of time in sales in my life, and I learned that there are three types of customers: a dissatisfied customer, a satisfied customer, and a more than satified customer. The more than satisfied person will tell usually 3 to 5 people about their experience. A satisfied person might tell 1 or 2 people at most, but a dissatisfied customer will tell everyone they know. This is what you have, a guy who's completely dissatisfied, and is using every resource available to him to carry out his mission. Pretty much anyone I know would do the same thing. Disclaimers, lack of knowledge of the situation, excuses and reasons don't serve to satisfy the problem. Now about all you can do is damage control. I hope you guys can work this out.<BR>~Taiji<p>[This message has been edited by Taijiguy (edited 04-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000035||TRL46202||04-24-2001||12:04 PM||||The fact is he sent back the seat covers based on what Terry said about returns?? If Terry works, acts, speaks for George, George needs to make it known to his "friends" what his policy is. George, he sent the seat covers back and if you say that they are in great condition then you can sell them to someone else. Give him his money back and stop this!! Your a business man, act like one, and don't fuel the fire by stating your comments to forum members that you have or never have done business with. Watch what you say to people and remember you are talking to a very large Fiero family. <P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000036||c m west||04-24-2001||12:23 PM||||how about everyone here quit being nosy and let Goerge and Jamie figure it out - I know I certainly dont care to hear it all, and how can I possibly benifit from hearing this drama, ****  - Im only 21 and its like hearing a bunch of girls bickering at each other over who wore what in high school.....<P>So George, Jaime - here is your chance to talk this all out - and I suggest using a phone so as to not feed the rumor hungry forum.<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000037||Voytek||04-24-2001||12:32 PM||||GodSend: agreed 100%.  That's what the Forum is for.  If the Fiero Shop satisfies Jamie (A CUSTOMER), than I sincerely hope we see this resolution on the Forum.  Selling Fiero parts to enthusiasts does not warrant poor customer service (whether true in this case or not).<BR>84Bill: agreed 100%.  Opinions is what this Forum is about.  We all have an opinion about the Fiero and that's why we're here.<BR>So here's my opinion (and an answer to RobertVol):<BR>About a month ago I contacted the Fiero Shop via e-mail regarding a 3.1 conversion asking if it'll work, what to watch out for and for any tips since I know they have done this.  I guess I wasn't buying anything at the time, so the reply was this: 'You guys on the Forum seem to know a lot.  It'll work'.  (??????!!!!!!)  Allow me to translate: 'Quit bothering me 'cause I don't have time for people who aren't buying anything'.  Thanks for the help Fiero Shop - I assure you I won't be needing any parts from you for my Fieros.<BR>88Formula: I think even a WalMart guy would feel somewhat obligated to try to help a potential customer.<p>[This message has been edited by Voytek (edited 04-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000038||JAMIE||04-24-2001||12:37 PM||||To all those who responded,both negatively or positively, thank you for your comments.<P>To Cliff, sorry about the second thread.I see your point - the usage of a second thread rather than continuation of an existing thread was due to my ignorance of Forum rules.<P>Several respondents raised the point about contacting George.It may well be true that, had I contacted him instead of Terry, this whole mess could have been avoided.I contacted Terry because he was the only person I dealt with when I purchased the seat covers and because I thought, based on Terry's postings on the Forum, that he was one of the owners of The Fiero Shop. I was acting on the best information I had and was chasing a considerable sum of money. Those of you who know George and suggested I should have contacted him are probably quite correct but you have a distinct advantage over me - the advantage is that you know George and/or his position in the Fiero Shop - having dealt only with Terry it is reasonable to expect that I would pursue him rather than someone I know nothing about.<P>George has now emailed me directly and we have traded emails.He has noted above that he will deal with this issue directly with me and has asked me to call him.This is a reasonable request and I will indeed call George.<P>Jamie<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000039||RobertVol||04-24-2001||02:30 PM||||Jamie glad the hear that you guys are getting the problem fixed. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Now to the point that I was making about making the comment about George. He helped me out and "AT THE TIME" Jamie was not happy. The reason for the post I made was to show By one thread people will start saying "I wont use this guy" which is a BIG mistake!!!<P>By one post you won't buy from this guy!??!?<P>How do you know they there isnt more to the story?  Maybe not in this case but in others I can guarantee you there was more than suspected bad service, there was something personal involved in the POSTS that were made. Somebody was trying to make someone look bad. NOT in THIS POST BUT IN OTHERS<P>And to prove my point in reponse to Voyteks response about the Fierostore... He had a problem with them hmmmmm<P>Would anyone like us to pull all the "Good"Posts on the forum about Fierostore? I guarantee they out weight the bad<P>Question......................<BR>How many will stop buying because of his bad issue.....? Huh Yeah That what I thought.  <P>Anyway, This is a public forum so everyone has a right to their opinion<P>God bless America! <P>OUT! ||||reg||1
