Z||000044||Cliff Pennock||04-24-2001||03:57 PM||||I'm glad this is (going to be) resolved.<P>RobertVol: about your rating idea, it's actually something I've been working out for quite some time now. The only problem I'm having is how to keep it from being abused. Someone who holds a grudge against a particular vendor can single-handedly create a very low rating (and vice-versa, a vendor can create a high rating). Ebay doesn't have this problem since you need to be registered in order to rate someone else, and a creditcard is required for registration.<P>So I'm thinking more in the line of enabling people to leave their comments. But problem remains that most happy customers are happy in silence, while unhappy customers want the world to know.<P>For those asking why I didn't close this thread: I didn't do so because I believe everybody has a right to hear how this thing ends. We are all potential customers and while George is right that what is discussed between him and Jamie is private, I do feel it <B>is</B> our business to know what the end result is.<P>That said, I do not believe any of the vendors that hang out here are out to screw us. This community is simply too big for that. Screw one forum member here and you'll loose thousands of potential customers. The registered number of members is actually only a small part of the Fiero-owners visiting here. My guess is that for every registered member, there are at least 3 other fiero owners who regularly visit the forum, but are not registered. My log files tell me that much.<P>I want to say something else in defense of the Fiero Shop. Some people think that since their prices are very high, they must be making a fortune on all the parts they are selling. Well, first of all, from what I read here on the forum, the parts are usually in excellent condition. That's worth something. "But I can get the same part in excellent condition from another forum-member here, and for much less", I hear you say. Sure, but I bet that forum-member doesn't have a huge storage space to make sure all those parts <B>stay</B> in excellent condition, even if they need to be stored for years. I know, since I sell computerparts, that storing non-current parts is expensive. <B>Very</B> expensive. I'd rather use the space for more current stuff, but in order to keep my customers happy, I need to store that old stuff too. It's all part of doing business.<P>Right, I'll step of my soapbox now.||||reg||1
Z||000045||RobertVol||04-24-2001||04:30 PM||||he he CLiff ....I just mentioned it to see if you were listening!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000046||Cliff Pennock||04-24-2001||04:33 PM||||I'm <B>always</B> listening (or at least pretending I am).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000047||JAMIE||04-25-2001||11:08 AM||||Robertvol - thank you for the additional comments, I understand your point.<P>Just to let everyone know, George and I have resolved this issue in a satisfactory manner.There were basically 2 simple problems here - The Fiero Shop inadvertently overlooked my credit for the returned parts and I was chasing the wrong person; both were innocent mistakes.<P>I have learned a valuable lesson from all of this - if you have a problem,make absolutely sure you are dealing with the appropriate person.<P>One final comment: to their credit, both Terry and George were very courteous and professional during my telephone conversations with them yesterday and today.This is usually not typical in an adversarial situation and it made the resolution process much simpler.<P>Jamie<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000048||2xsess||04-25-2001||11:20 AM||||Thank God that's over.<P>Glad to hear you got it resovled Jamie.<P>Hopefully the positive ending will help negate some of the sour comment made towards the Fiero Shop.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>  <B>*For Sale*<BR>        $2000obo</B>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">        <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>Visit My Website</A>||||reg||10
Z||000049||Oreif||04-25-2001||11:51 AM||||Glad everything worked out. In my past dealings with George, He was always helpful and seem the type of person not to lose his temper. <P>As for vendor rating, Cliff, what about doing it so that the rating could show the registered members name, a thumbs up or thumbs down, and maybe an 80 character/one line comment. That way if it is abused, you'll know right away. Maybe even a second line so the particular vendor can comment/reply. That may also stop the "bad customer" side also. (Although we don't have any bad vendors or customers here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  )<P>Just a thought.<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||14
