Z||000052||Firestarter_87||04-25-2001||04:48 PM||||I can't believe how idiotic and childish most of you are.  How can a problem get resolved if it is not brought to the attention of all parties involved?  While it is unreasonible to expect one to completely exhaust all outlets before bringing a problem to a public forum, it is reasonible that one at least attempts to resolve a problem first.  Granted, one e-mail was sent to Terry, that does not qualify as an attempt.  <P>The saddening part of this entire situation is that it will cause the Fiero Shop much money in lost business due to bad PR.  Let me ask you Fiero Shop bashers this question, what Fiero related business has consistantly better prices when compared to the Fiero Shop?  Many times Fiero owners, always looking to stretch their pennies, will claim that they found parts cheaper from a private seller.  Of course, a business by definition is meant to make at least some money.  I do not feel that the Fiero Shop, Fiero Store, Fiero Factory, Rodney Dickman, Paul McKibben or V8 Archie gouge their customers.  In fact, many of their services are provided at a cost that cannot and will not heavily pad their pockets.  <P>DISCLAIMER: I am not in any way linked to the Fiero Shop.  I have purchased a clutch from them and am extremely happy with its build quality and construction.  Furthermore, much like The Fiero Factory, George cannot charge enough for his knowledge which usually comes freely.  <P>Firestarter<P>Edited to ask another question... Do you not think that George would make more money leaving catering to imports (like Ryane did)?<p>[This message has been edited by Firestarter_87 (edited 04-25-2001).]||||reg||1
