Z||000054||Raydar||04-25-2001||05:52 PM||||I'm glad this is resolved, too. <BR>Based upon what I've heard about George and the Fiero Shop, I really wouldn't have expected anything different. <BR>It is only human nature to assume the worst, and jump to conclusions, based upon those assumptions. <BR>I am the world's worst at this. I'm always looking for the dark cloud inside the silver lining. <P>Peace!<P>Raydar||||reg||6
Z||000055||jlruiz67||04-25-2001||07:52 PM||||I'm glad this discussion started here and we got to see the results. This is why I like this forum. I now have a more respect for the Fiero Shop than I had before (and I did have a great deal of respect for George after talking to him in San Diego last year). George took care of the situation once brought to his attention and we all benefited from the exchange. Now I think, to be honest, most people can see this discussion as a plus for the Fiero Shop for the handling of the situation.||||reg||14
Z||000056||RobertVol||04-25-2001||09:54 PM||||Let me say <P>1. GREAT! Glad to see that everything worked out for Jamie<P>2. Let me say I really believe in using this Forum for Vendor issues, just that, as I have said, it needs to be "CONTROLLED" to keep from Personal issues being included. If thats possible. Cliff, I hope you and all of us can put our ideas together and come up with something. Believe it or not even though there may be bad vendors out there...."God Forbid!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   I honestly don't think many reside on the Forum. Cliff seems to monitor complaints and issues like this pretty well and if he saw an issue I think he would remove them.<P>3. Ain't this FORUM GREAT!!!????!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>Again I am glad it was resolved....<P>All is well in the Forum universe ! <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club<P>CLICK BELOW AND SEE OUR SITE !!! <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=819451&a=5959473&p=36934984&Sequence=1">  <p>[This message has been edited by RobertVol (edited 04-25-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000057||JAMIE||04-26-2001||07:50 AM||||Firestarter,<P>You commented that one email to Terry would not constitute an attempt to resolve the issue. I agree. Please be assured I did make a valid attempt and this was not a case of a single email.<P>I respectfully disagree with your comment that most Forum members are idiotic and childish.Occasionally people feel very strongly about a particular issue and their emotions become visible in their response - this is human nature.There were a variety of opinions expressed in this thread and many of the "negative" responses still had very good points contained therein.I thought,by and large, that the vast majority of responses in this thread were well written and certainly well intentioned - I appreciated all of them even if I disagree with some of them - I appreciated your post as well - your basic message contains some valid points, but the comment about Forum members is, in my opinion and based on my experiences in this Forum, not valid. It's ok to disagree over issues and with members comments - just as you may disagree with the comments I am now making - this is an integral part of the Forum.<P>Jamie<P>||||reg||1
Z||000058||Firestarter_87||04-27-2001||11:37 AM||||JAMIE,<P>Please note that your experiences on the Forum have been relatively short.  I have been reading and posting on this Forum (albeit under another user name) for two years.  My opinions of the majority of the members has been constantly evolving over that time period.  In the beginning there were few members, but the caliber of the average member was much higher.  Today the forum is overcrowded with mental midgets.  Almost every day we have some huge, blown out of porportion scandal such as this.  Please note that I am not saying that you are unintelligent in any way, I am merely pointing out the trend of the forum "dumbing down".  <P>Firestarter||||reg||1
Z||000059||Voytek||04-27-2001||03:09 PM||||Firestarter - hmm, a very suiting name.  What you call scandals, others would call differences of opinion.  I don't know what other name you used to post under, but in my OPINION this declining 'caliber' of members is in part contributed to by 'experienced' members such as yourself (if you've been here as long as you claim you have).  Some of the controversial views make for a more exciting forum.  The potential that any one of us will express their satisfaction or dissatisfaction with a vendor on the forum, only keeps the vendors more honest.  Next time before you label everyone here (or most people) idiots and children, STOP AND GIVE YOUR HEAD A SHAKE FIRST!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
